# tools/c/convergence_prove_witness.rish -- one prover where twenty-seven hand-written cases were owed.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/c/convergence_prove_witness.rish
#
# `tools/c/convergence_census.sh` measured 30 tools writing to the tracked tree with 3 proving they
# converge. The obvious repair was to hand-write a convergence case into each of the other 27
# controls -- which is the census's own finding performed once per tool: a rule kept where a hand
# remembered. **22 of the 27 share one invocation shape**, a single file path, so one prover answers
# for all of them and the five that differ are named rather than skipped in silence.
#
# WHAT IT PROVES is narrow and is the tree's own claim: running a writer twice on a copy leaves the
# file byte-identical to what one run left -- `infusion(world') -> world'`.
#
# THE THIRD VERDICT IS THE ONE THAT MATTERS. `inert` says the FIRST run changed nothing, so the
# sample exercised no path and the reading proves nothing. A sample that triggers no work is the
# quiet way a convergence proof lies, and the control plants exactly that case.

say "convergence-prove: Language EN -- one instrument for a property twenty-seven tools claim."
say "convergence-prove: Style Gauge, Meter -- three verdicts, and the honest one is named."
say "convergence-prove: Lens TAME -- safety first: the subject is a copy, never the tree."

say "convergence-prove: the control -- eighteen behaviors, including a tool built to diverge and two second-run refusals..."
let ctl = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/c/convergence_prove_control.sh"]
assert ctl.ok else "convergence-prove: the control refused --\n${ctl.out}\n${ctl.err}"
assert ctl.out contains "pass=18 fail=0" else "convergence-prove: the control did not prove eighteen behaviors --\n${ctl.out}\n${ctl.err}"

# invariant: the control exercises the prover against a TRACKED writer on a real sample, not only
# against tools it invented, and asserts the reading is `converges` rather than `inert` -- a green
# built on an inert sample is the lie that verdict exists to prevent.
assert ctl.out contains "coverage: a tracked tree writer was exercised on a real sample, and both second-run refusals -- one holding the file, one writing before it refused -- were told apart" else "convergence-prove: the control never exercised a tracked writer"

say "GREEN: convergence-prove -- a writer run twice on a copy, with divergence caught, both second-run refusals told apart, and an inert sample refused as proof."
